gh the Calculus Gallery must be brief, and we can stop only oc- ... 2z2 + 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThomaesche Funktion (https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomaesche_Funktion)\nciteturn981search15 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 1.4 years ago; Zitiert nach William Dunham: The Calculus Gallery: Masterpieces from Newton to Lebesgue.Princeton University Press, 2004, ISBN 978-0-691-09565-3, Chapter 10.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHenri Lebesgue (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henri_Lebesgue)\nciteturn981search16 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; Henri Léon Lebesgue (; ; June 28, 1875 – July 26, 1941) was a French mathematician known for his theory of integration, which was a generalization of the 17th-century concept of integration—summing the area between an axis and the curve of a function defined for that axis. ... Between March 1899 and April 1901 Lebesgue published six notes in Comptes Rendus. ... Lebesgue's great thesis, Intégrale, longueur, aire, with the full account of this work, appeared in the Annali di Matematica in 1902.The first chapter develops the theory of measure (see Borel measure). ... In a 1910 paper, \"Représentation trigonométrique approchée des fonctions satisfaisant a une condition de Lipschitz\" deals with the Fourier series of functions satisfying a Lipschitz condition, with an evaluation of the order of magnitude of the remainder term. ... This surprising relationship between two major geometric operations in calculus, differentiation and integration, is now known as the fundamental theorem of calculus.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWilliam Dunham (https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Dunham)\nciteturn981search17 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 8 months ago; Dunham a reçu de l'American Association of Publishers la récompense du Best Mathematics Book 1994 pour son livre . ... * (en) The